🔧 Lab Setup
Step 1: Install Virtualization Software

Download and install Oracle VM VirtualBox from its official website:

https://www.virtualbox.org/

VirtualBox provides the virtualization platform required to create and manage the lab machines.

Step 2: Obtain Operating Systems

The operating systems used in this project were obtained from their respective official sources.

Linux: https://www.kali.org/get-kali/
Windows: https://www.microsoft.com/software-download/

Ensure that operating system licensing requirements are followed when installing and using the virtual machines.

Step 3: Create the Virtual Machines

Create two separate virtual machines in VirtualBox:

Linux — Attacker Machine
Windows — Target Machine

Allocate appropriate memory, processor resources, and virtual storage according to the available host hardware.

Step 4: Configure the Internal Network

Configure the network adapter of both virtual machines using the following settings:

VirtualBox → Settings → Network → Adapter 1

Enable Network Adapter: Yes
Attached to: Internal Network
Network Name: CyberLab

Ensure that both machines use the same Internal Network name.

This configuration allows the virtual machines to communicate within the designated virtual network while keeping the lab separate from the host's normal network connection.

Step 5: Verify Network Connectivity

After starting both virtual machines:

Identify the IP address assigned to each machine.
Verify that both systems belong to the intended virtual network.
Test connectivity between the machines.
Document the network configuration for future reference.

Network configuration and connectivity should be verified before beginning any security assessment.
